custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T02:25:42-08:00","id":793029,"title":"","content":"Listening to this now and I'm really enjoying it, however I have to disagree with you guys on a rather important point.<br /> <br /> Around the 16:40 mark you say that there are only 7th generation Daughters running around. However, the V20 core book strongly implies there are multiple sixth generation daughters running around. This implies that their founder is of the 5th generation.<br /> <br /> Page 454 - in the section on Persistant Echo, the 7th level power of Melpominee<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Multiple Daughters may use this Discipline in concert. </div> </div> </div>Page 202 - in the section on Spectral Visage, the 7th level power of Protean<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although his lungs are no longer solid, the vampire can<br /> still speak, a fact in which some elders of the Daughters<br /> of Cacophony bloodline have expressed great interest. </div> </div> </div>As for their origin, I'd just have them be a product of a mixed embrace of a Malkavian Methuselah and a Toreador or Ventrue Methuselah. Could have been lovers, could have been an experiment, either willing or not.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Presence 6: Melusine's Song is an awesome discipline choice for a Daughter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This power grants a vampire the ability to sway another through song. If the Artisan can phrase her requests in song form, those words can take on the power of nigh-irresistible commands.<br /> <br /> ... <b>knowledge of this power reduces the difficulty by 1 of all rolls related to singing.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 12-26-2015, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}